From: Crunch41 <70764418+Crunch41@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 04:01:20 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Run the dedicated room unattended

The standalone room waits for input on stdin ("Close with Q+Enter") and
has no signal handling. In a container stdin is closed, so the wait loop
spins on std::cin, and docker stop's SIGTERM kills the process before it
stops announcing the room, saves the ban list or closes the room.

- Replace the stdin loop with a once-a-second check of the room state and
  a flag set by SIGINT and SIGTERM. Stopping the process now runs the
  normal shutdown path: ban list save, announce cleanup, room Destroy().
  The ban list is saved before the room unregisters from the lobby,
  which waits on the network: a stop that runs out of time (docker stop
  allows 10 seconds) then can't lose the bans.
- --username takes a required argument. With optional_argument,
  "--username name" left optarg null and crashed when it was read.

Tests: the image's startup/shutdown check and tests/test_room_protocol.py
stop the room with SIGTERM and require a clean exit, not a kill, and
that a public room writes its ban list when it stops.
---
 src/dedicated_room/yuzu_room.cpp | 35 ++++++++++++++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/dedicated_room/yuzu_room.cpp b/src/dedicated_room/yuzu_room.cpp
index 824fd0f26c8892aec1d4d6c1a117b50492843ef3..b9142525fda077d65c99ed3c2e0475893f34962c 100644
--- a/src/dedicated_room/yuzu_room.cpp
+++ b/src/dedicated_room/yuzu_room.cpp
@@ -7,7 +7,9 @@
 // SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright yuzu/Citra Emulator Project
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
 
+#include <atomic>
 #include <chrono>
+#include <csignal>
 #include <fstream>
 #include <iostream>
 #include <memory>
@@ -81,6 +83,14 @@ static constexpr char BanListMagic[] = "YuzuRoom-BanList-1";
 
 static constexpr char token_delimiter{':'};
 
+namespace {
+std::atomic_bool g_shutdown_requested{false};
+
+void HandleShutdownSignal(int) {
+    g_shutdown_requested.store(true);
+}
+} // namespace
+
 static void PadToken(std::string& token) {
     std::array<unsigned char, 512> output{};
     std::array<unsigned char, 2048> roundtrip{};
@@ -203,7 +213,7 @@ void LaunchRoom(int argc, char** argv, bool called_by_option) {
         {"password", required_argument, 0, 'w'},
         {"preferred-game", required_argument, 0, 'g'},
         {"preferred-game-id", required_argument, 0, 'i'},
-        {"username", optional_argument, 0, 'u'},
+        {"username", required_argument, 0, 'u'},
         {"token", required_argument, 0, 't'},
         {"web-api-url", required_argument, 0, 'a'},
         {"ban-list-file", required_argument, 0, 'b'},
@@ -219,6 +229,9 @@ void LaunchRoom(int argc, char** argv, bool called_by_option) {
     Common::Log::SetColorConsoleBackendEnabled(true);
     Common::Log::Start();
 
+    std::signal(SIGINT, HandleShutdownSignal);
+    std::signal(SIGTERM, HandleShutdownSignal);
+
     while (optind < argc) {
         int arg = getopt_long(argc, argv, "n:d:s:p:m:w:g:u:t:a:i:l:hv", long_options, &option_index);
         if (arg != -1) {
@@ -366,27 +379,23 @@ void LaunchRoom(int argc, char** argv, bool called_by_option) {
             LOG_INFO(Network, "Failed to create room: ");
             std::exit(-1);
         }
-        LOG_INFO(Network, "Room is open. Close with Q+Enter...");
+        LOG_INFO(Network, "Room is open. Stop the process to close it cleanly.");
         auto announce_session = std::make_unique<Core::AnnounceMultiplayerSession>();
         if (announce) {
             announce_session->Start();
         }
-        while (room->GetState() == Network::Room::State::Open) {
-            std::string in;
-            std::cin >> in;
-            if (in.size() > 0) {
-                break;
-            }
-            std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(100));
+        while (room->GetState() == Network::Room::State::Open && !g_shutdown_requested.load()) {
+            std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::seconds(1));
+        }
+        // Save the ban list first: unregistering from the lobby below waits on the network,
+        // and a stop that runs out of time (docker stop allows 10 seconds) must not lose bans.
+        if (!ban_list_file.empty()) {
+            SaveBanList(room->GetBanList(), ban_list_file);
         }
         if (announce) {
             announce_session->Stop();
         }
         announce_session.reset();
-        // Save the ban list
-        if (!ban_list_file.empty()) {
-            SaveBanList(room->GetBanList(), ban_list_file);
-        }
         room->Destroy();
     }
     Network::Shutdown();
